    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: deterministic `householdId`\n\nThe `householdId` is now the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`, so owners with the same last name and postcode share it automatically \u2014 `sharesHousehold` no longer *creates* the link, it only *bypasses the duplicate block*.\n\n### Files changed\n\n**`OwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 rewritten as the single source of the deterministic id. Replaced the old member-lookup/opt-in logic (`resolve`, `matchingMembers`, `existingId`, `deriveId`) with two pure functions, `householdId(OwnerFieldsDto)` and `householdId(Owner)`, both computing `SHA-256(normalizedLastName|postcode)` truncated to 12 hex chars. No longer keys on address.\n\n**`AssignOwnerHousehold.java`** \u2014 now unconditionally assigns `owner.setHouseholdId(OwnerHousehold.householdId(request))` to every owner (no repository lookup, no `sharesHousehold` gate).\n\n**`CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 duplicate detection keyed off the computed id. Rejects 409 when either the whole identity key matches (exact duplicate) **or** an existing owner shares the household (same computed `householdId`) \u2014 the household branch bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold`. Computes each existing owner's household id on the fly, so it's robust to seed rows that have a null stored id.\n\n**`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 now takes the request; a declared household member (`sharesHousehold` true) is never flagged as a possible duplicate.\n\n**`OwnerAddressNormalizer.java`** + **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 doc/spec text updated to describe the deterministic `(lastName, postcode)` keying and the declared-member exception.\n\n### On \"household-size input to the membership level\"\nI checked `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel` and the OpenAPI spec: membership level here is derived from email presence + `namesakeCount`, with no household-size input in this codebase \u2014 so there was nothing keyed off the household to redirect there. The concrete household consumers are duplicate detection and the possible-duplicate flag, both updated.\n\n### Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` passes (same lastName+postcode \u2192 equal `householdId`; different lastName \u2192 different id; the `sharesHousehold` owner is created rather than blocked). `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
